<p>Note: The company said its quarter's pre-tax earnings included gains of $2.5 million for accounting policy changes for ancillary linen revenue and $1.8 million from improved workers compensation experience.</p>
<p>The 1996 quarter included gains of $6.3 million from improved workers compensation claims experience.  </p>
<p>Analyst consensus for the quarter's earnings per share was $0.62, according to First Call.</p>
